    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "==Topic: {{ $('Duplicate Check').first().json.topic }}\n\nPost:\n{{ $json.output }}\n\nFraming for today: {{ ['top-down flat lay of the desk','close-up at desk level with a blurred background','over-the-shoulder angle showing only hands','wide corner shot of the whole workspace'][Math.floor(Math.random()*4)] }}\n\nWrite the image prompt.",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "==You write image prompts for the FLUX schnell model. The image goes on a LinkedIn post by a student learning cybersecurity and electronics. It must look like a real, relatable photo from a student's workspace, not stock art.\n\nVisual style to apply: {{ $('Config').first().json.imageStyle }}\n\nMethod: find the specific physical things the post is about (for example a router and ethernet cables, a breadboard with LEDs and a multimeter, a laptop showing a terminal window, a Raspberry Pi). Build one believable scene around them with a human touch: a mug of tea, a half-finished notebook sketch, hands typing or holding a probe, sticky notes, a slightly messy desk. The scene should tell a small story of someone mid-project, learning something.\n\nWrite ONE paragraph on a single line, 45-70 words, in plain descriptive language: main subject, supporting objects, setting, the given framing, camera and lens, lighting, colours, mood.\n\nRules: only things that can be photographed; no readable text, letters, numbers, signs or logos anywhere (screens show soft glow or blurred shapes only); no faces, hands only if people appear; avoid hooded hackers, padlocks, matrix code, neon robots, glossy 3D renders.\n\nReturn only the prompt."
        }
      },
